    "readme": "Rocket remains READ_ONLY_RESEARCH_ONLY_HUMAN_GATED.\n\nMission: Determine whether a scientifically defensible BTC derivatives strategy can identify rare attractive directional momentum opportunities, enter efficiently, manage deterministically and express through futures/options, or terminate with negative evidence.\n\nThis Project is a decision tree. Every primary work item has unlock/success/failure/kill conditions. WIP = 3 unique research work items (In Progress + Review / Gate); linked PRs are evidence for those items, not extra research admissions. Healthy operational services do not consume WIP.\n\nMOM-000 is completed: STOP_INSUFFICIENT_FEASIBILITY; MOM-001 not admitted; predictive trials zero. #49 contains reconciliation and CFTC corrections pending independent acceptance. MOM-002 is Draft in this program despite its frozen reviewable proposal in #49: no fitting, association inspection or scoring. Accepted #51 foundation/Tier-B/overlap + accepted #58 pre-outcome power audit -> #56 near-term human decisions and finalized pre-result contract -> #54 independent exact final-packet review -> official admission/freeze -> code gate/audit. MOM-002 is Draft/NEEDS_PRE_RESULT_GATE_REVIEW, unapproved/unadmitted/unscored. Conditional synthetic findings do not amend gates or consume a predictive trial. FAIL rejects the entire parked downstream branch; no MOM-003 rescue. PASS needs human acknowledgment before only the next separately admitted phase is decomposed. Data only for admitted work or existing correctness bugs.\n\nTerminal states: STRATEGY_VALIDATED -> READY_FOR_CAPITAL_REVIEW (agents stop; capital requires human authorization), or RESEARCH_LINE_REJECTED (preserve negative evidence and stop). Reviewer/process, 40bp appropriateness, minimum worthwhile effect and post-audit terminal/descriptive economics remain human decisions. STOP/no-MOM-003 is confirmed by the human mandate. #59 downstream risk/capital charter remains Parked until audited historical PASS acknowledged by human; MOM-002 FAIL rejects it. #60 tracks real identity separation; shared @jhonnyisaacc proves no scientific independence.\n\nGovernance source: docs/research/AUTONOMOUS_RESEARCH_PROTOCOL.md via dedicated governance PR. Historical PRs remain evidence; do not merge runtime changes to preserve documents. Main must require PR/review/CI and forbid force pushes. Project fields summarize authority; committed contracts and code gates govern outcomes.\n\nReview tiers: MAINTENANCE (tests/CI/separate code review; #52/#55), FOUNDATION (independent technical/adversarial #51/#58), SCIENTIFIC_ADMISSION (isolated no-result exact-artifact #53/#54), PROSPECTIVE_VALIDATION, CAPITAL (human only). Trial Budget differs from Trials Consumed: #53 1/0; #58 0/0. Primary membership and committed policy govern dispatch; unrelated Rocket issues and historical PRs never compete for WIP.\n\nPR dispositions: #57/#49 MERGE_WHEN_ACCEPTED, #57 first then #51 acceptance/#49 governed-main update/review. #26/#38/#40/#46/#50 CLOSE_EVIDENCE_ARCHIVE only after individual preservation, archive label and closing note; #50 after #51, note references #49/#51. All remain open pending blockers; no agent self-merge. Final frozen MOM-002 FAIL rejects entire downstream branch; no MOM-003 rescue.\n",
    "shortDescription": "Gated BTC derivatives research. WIP 3. Preserve failures; no rescue; read-only and human-gated.",
    "title": "Rocket \u2014 Derivatives Strategy Research",
    "url": "https://github.com/users/jhonnyisaacc/projects/4"
